    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<img width=\"864\" height=\"1296\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Mischief_Lisa-Nasson.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Mischief_Lisa-Nasson.webp?w=864&amp;ssl=1 864w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Mischief_Lisa-Nasson.webp?resize=200%2C300&amp;ssl=1 200w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Mischief_Lisa-Nasson.webp?resize=683%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 683w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Mischief_Lisa-Nasson.webp?resize=768%2C1152&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Mischief_Lisa-Nasson.webp?resize=640%2C960&amp;ssl=1 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 864px) 100vw, 864px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/lisanasson\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFacebook\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M504 256C504 119 393 8 256 8S8 119 8 256c0 123.78 90.69 226.38 209.25 245V327.69h-63V256h63v-54.64c0-62.15 37-96.48 93.67-96.48 27.14 0 55.52 4.84 55.52 4.84v61h-31.28c-30.8 0-40.41 19.12-40.41 38.73V256h68.78l-11 71.69h-57.78V501C413.31 482.38 504 379.78 504 256z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lisanasson?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&#038;igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tInstagram\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M224.1 141c-63.6 0-114.9 51.3-114.9 114.9s51.3 114.9 114.9 114.9S339 319.5 339 255.9 287.7 141 224.1 141zm0 189.6c-41.1 0-74.7-33.5-74.7-74.7s33.5-74.7 74.7-74.7 74.7 33.5 74.7 74.7-33.6 74.7-74.7 74.7zm146.4-194.3c0 14.9-12 26.8-26.8 26.8-14.9 0-26.8-12-26.8-26.8s12-26.8 26.8-26.8 26.8 12 26.8 26.8zm76.1 27.2c-1.7-35.9-9.9-67.7-36.2-93.9-26.2-26.2-58-34.4-93.9-36.2-37-2.1-147.9-2.1-184.9 0-35.8 1.7-67.6 9.9-93.9 36.1s-34.4 58-36.2 93.9c-2.1 37-2.1 147.9 0 184.9 1.7 35.9 9.9 67.7 36.2 93.9s58 34.4 93.9 36.2c37 2.1 147.9 2.1 184.9 0 35.9-1.7 67.7-9.9 93.9-36.2 26.2-26.2 34.4-58 36.2-93.9 2.1-37 2.1-147.8 0-184.8zM398.8 388c-7.8 19.6-22.9 34.7-42.6 42.6-29.5 11.7-99.5 9-132.1 9s-102.7 2.6-132.1-9c-19.6-7.8-34.7-22.9-42.6-42.6-11.7-29.5-9-99.5-9-132.1s-2.6-102.7 9-132.1c7.8-19.6 22.9-34.7 42.6-42.6 29.5-11.7 99.5-9 132.1-9s102.7-2.6 132.1 9c19.6 7.8 34.7 22.9 42.6 42.6 11.7 29.5 9 99.5 9 132.1s2.7 102.7-9 132.1z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Mischief&nbsp;by Lisa Nasson </h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p>Tuesday, September 23rd – Sunday, October 12th | 2:00 PM (weekends only) &amp; 7:30 PM</p>\n<p>Pay-What-You-Can performance on Tuesday, September 23rd | 7:30 PM&nbsp;<br>\nMasked performance on Sunday, October 5th | 2:00pm</p>\n<p><a style=\"color: #ded9e9;\" href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/accessibility/#neptune\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Neptune Theatre – Scotiabank Studio Stage</a></p>\n<p>A Co-Production by Neptune Theatre, Native Earth Performing Arts, &amp; Tarragon Theatre</p>\n<p>In support of Neptune Theatre</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/Untitled-design-4-PhotoRoom.png-PhotoRoom-e1720715251990-300x140.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"170\" height=\"79\"></p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://sales.neptunetheatre.com/Online/default.asp?BOparam::WScontent::loadArticle::permalink=Mischief&#038;BOparam::WScontent::loadArticle::context_id=&#038;_gl=1*6wjhi7*_gcl_au*MTYyNzI4NzkwNC4xNzQ5NjQ1OTA5*_ga*MTc0MDI4NTg5NC4xNzUwMTY2OTQ5*_ga_8982X81KS0*czE3NTQ5MTk4MzQkbzExJGcxJHQxNzU0OTE5ODcxJGoyMyRsMCRoMjAyNjczMTg3Nw..&#038;_ga=2.262074952.471844064.1754919834-1740285894.1750166949\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tBuy Tickets  \n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Mischief</h2>\t\t\t\t\n\t\tThis gentle comedy asks the question - how can a woman whose family lives in a society placed under a microscope of stereotype, carry the resilience of her ancestors to embrace their existence?Between mystical visits from an ancient ancestor, every-day life at her job at her Uncle's convenience store on the Rez, and her community rallying to tear down a statue of her city's founder, Brooke feels torn. She is struggling to reconcile her Mi'kmaw heritage and living in a place founded by a British military officer hell bent on destroying her ancestors.\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Personnel</h2>\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><strong>Lisa Nasson</strong> | Brooke<br /><strong>Yolanda Bonnell</strong> | Emily<br /><strong>Devin MacKinnon</strong> | Good Guy / Fisherman Fred<br /><strong>Trina Morgan</strong> | Tammy<br /><strong>Jeremy Proulx</strong> | Uncle Chris</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"1449\" height=\"1449\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Lisa-Nasson.jpeg\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Lisa-Nasson.jpeg?w=1449&amp;ssl=1 1449w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Lisa-Nasson.jpeg?resize=300%2C300&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Lisa-Nasson.jpeg?resize=1024%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Lisa-Nasson.jpeg?resize=150%2C150&amp;ssl=1 150w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Lisa-Nasson.jpeg?resize=768%2C768&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Lisa-Nasson.jpeg?resize=1120%2C1120&amp;ssl=1 1120w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Lisa-Nasson.jpeg?resize=640%2C640&amp;ssl=1 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1449px) 100vw, 1449px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Lisa Nasson</h2>\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p>Lisa Nasson is a Mi’kmaq Actor, Director and Teacher from Millbrook First Nation in Nova Scotia. Lisa attended Neptune Theatre’s Professional program, and George Brown Theatre School where she studied Acting and Performance Studies. Lisa has also been an arts educator for many years, in subjects of acting, comedy and musical theatre at the Neptune Theatre School, and Young People’s Theatre. She has been working as an actor since leaving George Brown College, and is excited to jump into a new area of the theatre business. Some of her recent theatre credits include, <em>Offensive Fouls</em> (Neptune Theatre), <em>Vivaldi’s Ring of Mystery</em> (Neptune Theatre), <em>Spirit Horse</em> (Roseneath Theatre), <em>Munschtime!</em> (Young Peoples Theatre), <em>Lullaby</em> (Eastern Front Theatre), and <em>Fatty Legs</em> (Xara Choral Theatre).</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/prismatic-2025/\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2025\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
      }
    ],
